/* book Worked example 2: Q: The shunt arm of the same T network gets a current-controlled voltage source 2I₁ (2 Ω × I₁) in series with its 4 Ω resistor, adding to the voltage across that arm. Find the Z parameters and test reciprocity.
   1. Centre-node voltage: the arm carries I₁ + I₂, so Vc = 4(I₁ + I₂) + 2I₁ = 6I₁ + 4I₂.
   2. V₁ = 2I₁ + Vc = 8I₁ + 4I₂, so z₁₁ = 8 Ω and z₁₂ = 4 Ω.
   3. V₂ = 3I₂ + Vc = 6I₁ + 7I₂, so z₂₁ = 6 Ω and z₂₂ = 7 Ω.
   4. z₁₂ = 4 Ω ≠ z₂₁ = 6 Ω: not reciprocal. In ABCD form AD − BC = z₁₂/z₂₁ = 4/6 = 0.667 ≠ 1, and in h form h₁₂ = 4/7 = 0.571 while −h₂₁ = 6/7 = 0.857.
   5. z₁₁ = 8 Ω ≠ z₂₂ = 7 Ω: not symmetric either.
   Answer: z₁₁ = 8 Ω, z₁₂ = 4 Ω, z₂₁ = 6 Ω, z₂₂ = 7 Ω; the dependent source makes the network non-reciprocal (AD − BC = 0.667). */
