/* book exam traps: Reciprocity is not symmetry. The T network is reciprocal (z₁₂ = z₂₁) but not symmetric (6 Ω ≠ 7 Ω). | In h and g parameters reciprocity carries a minus sign: h₁₂ = −h₂₁. Writing h₁₂ = h₂₁ fails every passive network. | AD − BC = 1 is the reciprocity test; A = D is the symmetry test. Swapping them is a common lost mark. | Symmetry in h form is Δh = 1, not Δh = 0 and not h₁₁ = h₂₂ (they do not even have the same unit). | Zin uses z₂₂ + ZL in the denominator and Zout uses z₁₁ + ZS. In ABCD form A and D swap places between Zin and Zout. */
